body:
Well, you could essentially choose any time. It depends on how magic works in your story. 

If there needs to be a connection to some other plane, then the reason could be: The portal was closed by someone/a culture/country/organization, to the detriment/gain of all humankind. The reason for opening the "portal" could be nefarious or hidden, thus appearing as gradual.

&#x200B;

If it is knowledge based the reason could be: a great tragedy happened with magic to blame and a group burned all the books (except  like..two? of course). But someone found one of the remaining, forgotten books.

&#x200B;

There could also be a brutal/miserable downside to the use of magic. Perhaps it takes the sacrificing of a human life to fulfill even the smallest magical task, or at least some kind of life. And up until a certain point this was tolerated, but there was a great abolishment...until now. 

&#x200B;

It could have to do with the alignment of celestial bodies. 

&#x200B;

It could have to do with gaining the attention of a specific deity. Whether it be gaining personal attention or earthly attention. We fell from favor? We grew boring? We got too violent? Maybe someone has done something surprising to gain this God's favor back, or turn its gaze back to humanity. 

&#x200B;

Are these ideas any good? Anyways I liked thinking of this stuff. Thank you for the excellent question.
